{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1722 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "dc307a2bbfef8c772e7a8f843294a4aefee3bc9af6849a195198207aa273ac2a" :edb/db-before-t 1721 :edb/db-after-t 1722 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535034 50 #inst "2026-10-08T15:16:40.623Z" 13194139535034 true] [17592186119754 1020 #edb/ref 17592186327829 13194139535034 true] [17592186119755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186327836 13194139535034 true] [17592186119755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186327843 13194139535034 true] [17592186119755 1020 #edb/ref 17592186327850 13194139535034 true] [17592186120181 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535034 true] [17592186120181 1100 "A nonzero vector $⟨a, b, 0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r \\cdot ⟨6,-2, 0⟩ =-14$. What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}$?" 13194139535034 false] [17592186120181 1100 "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩=-14.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" 13194139535034 true] [17592186120181 1145 "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩=-14$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨6,-2,0⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨6,-2,0⟩ & =0 \\\\ 6{t}_{1}-2{t}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =3{t}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},3{t}_{1},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ eqauls $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,3,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{1}{3}.$" 13194139535034 true] [17592186327829 1017 #edb/ref 17592186327830 13194139535034 true] [17592186327829 1089 "q-127888" 13194139535034 true] [17592186327829 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535034 true] [17592186327829 1100 "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,\\,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-1⟩=\\sqrt{2}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" 13194139535034 true] [17592186327829 1113 #uuid "f285e4c4-1506-574b-a01b-1dbc6576701f" 13194139535034 true] [17592186327829 1145 "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-1⟩=\\sqrt{2}$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨3,2,-1⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}-{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{3} & =3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,{t}_{2},\\,3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{2}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{2}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=\\frac{1}{2}.$" 13194139535034 true] [17592186327830 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327831 13194139535034 true] [17592186327830 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327832 13194139535034 true] [17592186327830 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327833 13194139535034 true] [17592186327830 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327834 13194139535034 true] [17592186327830 1000 #edb/ref 17592186327835 13194139535034 true] [17592186327830 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535034 true] [17592186327830 1041 "selection" 13194139535034 true] [17592186327830 1104 #edb/ref 17592186327833 13194139535034 true] [17592186327830 1110 #uuid "7889743d-327d-57bd-982e-9697f8fed55f" 13194139535034 true] [17592186327831 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139535034 true] [17592186327831 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535034 true] [17592186327831 1111 #uuid "d0424ac0-b370-5c08-84a3-dc6283867914" 13194139535034 true] [17592186327832 1034 "3" 13194139535034 true] [17592186327832 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535034 true] [17592186327832 1111 #uuid "a9d602b6-97bd-5178-9019-37c790a3279e" 13194139